<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13261" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēpŭdet</span></b> ,
			ŭit, 2, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. impers.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To be greatly ashamed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum eum non depuderet mare infestare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell.
					2, 73 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Not to be ashamed, to become shameless</i> (perh.
			not ante-Aug.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">very rare): depuduit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					4, 155</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">assiduis conviciis depudere didicerat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Const. Sap. 17</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
